David the Valkyrie (I randomize my characters without checking their
gender) somehow had my highest-ever score, with 6022332 points.  This
was interesting to me because she left her entire pile of gems and
artifacts (except for Mjollnir, her main weapon, and Fire Brand, her
backup) back in a stash on level 9.  She was near being burdened and I
decided that it was more important to me to ascend than to ascend with
a high score, so I left Sting and Orcrist and Trollsbane and a whole
pile of random, useless artifacts, plus all my gems.  I thought this
would affect my score a lot, but I still beat all my other ascended
characters (several wizards and 2 more valks).

  This game started out easily enough.  I didn't really get any
especially good luck in finding awesome armor, but I didn't find any
deadly-poisoned-spiked-pit traps on level 1 either (can they be
generated there?).  Oh well.  Being lawful, I upgraded my long sword to
Excalibur as soon as I reached lvl 5.  There were two unattended altars
on level 9, in adjacent rooms actually, and I used them to get Mjollnir
and all the intrinsics you can get by praying.  I didn't learn the
passcode though, or get protected.
  I had forgotten how easy the Valk quest is; the nemesis is like a
fire giant that just claims to be cooler than the rest of them.  I beat
him up and continued down.  By Medusa's level, I had a pair of
levitation boots so I wore them and went and stomped her.  Real
exciting.  I went for the Perseus statue, then realized that I had no
pickaxe :).  So I went all the way back to the Gnommish Mines and
killed peaceful dwarves that hit me with pickaxes to get one.  The
statue had a shield only, but I like to wear shields of reflection for
my valks, so I blessed it and carried it along.
  By the castle, I had somehow lost my levitation boots (hate it when
this happens, and it always does when I play really fast) and didn't
know the passtune.  At least I had a bugle from a soldier of some sort
on the level above.  I played it, and played it, and played it, and
crushed every single monster stupid enough to come out by the
drawbridge.  Then I went inside and crushed every single monster stupid
enough to not come out by the drawbridge.  I grabbed the WoW and got
myself Speed Boots, Gauntlets of Pwr, Frost Brand (my all-time favorite
weapon, gets double damage against basically any and every monster that
even kind of almost scares me), which I didn't get, and Fire Brand (I
needed something around besides Mjollnir.  The wand was still (1:1) at
this point.  I made myself some GDSM from a dragon's scales I had.  I
then penned myself a couple quick scrolls of genocide with a magic
marker I'd found and blessed them, wiping out h and L.  I do this every
game, because mind flayers kill me too fast (and I usually play wizards
so even if they don't kill me they hurt my spellcasting) and liches...
I've never faced an arch-lich and won; if I see one I just sprint for
my life upstairs and then genocide him.
  I went into Gehennom and started stomping stuff, but at some point
something killed my ring of teleport control, and I have teleportitis,
of course.  Wow that stunk.  I decided to level-port back up to my
stash and figure it out from there.  Oh wait, I can't control level
ports either.  I ended up on level 25 or so at least, and then went up
as fast as I could.  I finally made it (luckily I had just eaten a
black dragon right before the ring's death) and looked at my pile and
found a scroll of genocide.  It was uncursed, so I grabbed some water
and an old spell and a pile of scrolls of remove curse, and got lucky
on the 3rd try.  Dipped the scroll of genocide and called in tengus.
Almost all peaceful, but tough.  Killed and ate 3 or so before I got
intrinsic telecontrol.
  Not long after, something took out my ring of conflict.  That really
stunk, because there was no obvious method of getting that back.  It
was maddening because I'd found it only a level or so earlier but
forgotten to put it into my bag yet.
  The demon lords were not too exciting, but on Orcus' level I found no
less than 4 incubi lounging around.  My level went from 19 to 30 and my
HP from 240 to 500-something.  Anyway, I went to the bottom, marked the
Square, and started looking for Vlad's.  I always forget where it can
be so I checked every level, starting with the bottom, 47 (or 46.  not
too sure).  I finally found it on 30-something and whipped Vlad too.
Vlad had an AoLS lying around, as usual.
  Went back to minetown for candles, to the VS to drop the candles /
bell off.  Wandered until I found a ring of conflict and a pair of
jumping boots and a magic marker to enchant all my stuff.  Got all
ready, then went for the Wizard.  He woke up before I wanted him to,
and in the middle of my fight it took me a couple turns to figure out
he was standing there cursing all my stuff.  Oh well, read one of my 10
blessed scrolls of remove curse and then introduce him to my wand of
death.  I save remove curse and charging scrolls almost from the
beginning just for the ascension run, when I'm a Valk.
  Level-ported down and did the ritual.  Got lost in Moloch's Sanctum,
and ended up staying there longer than I meant to.  The Wizard showed
up again while I was still searching for the secret doors, but I didn't
really pay much attn to him.  I beat him up until he retreated, but I
didn't have the AoY yet and I did have remove curse scrolls so I wasn't
too massively worried.
  Finally made it through and found the wizard with the high priest.
Let them duke it out with conflict; the Wizard dbl-teamed and won.  I
whipped him and grabbed the Amulet.  Left again (no !oGL for me, didn't
feel like it was worth the trouble to curse one, partly because when I
thought of it I'd just blessed all my scrolls of remove curse.
  Luckily I had a ton of mana (I was careful to get my stats high early
and the incubi dancing I mentioned paid off) and I teleported to the
stairs of almost every level.  I ended up doing level 36 like 8 or 9
times in a row; it kept sending me back to who-knew where, but the
stupid level counter would never change... bleh.  Eventually I made it
through.  Oh, also at some point on this run Dispater showed up.  I
hadn't noticed him before (indeed, hadn't even seen him), probably
because he was peaceful and I hadn't worn conflict before?  I don't
know.  Anyway, got out of the dungeon pretty easily overall, except
that the OoF was heavy and, as I mentioned, I left all my gems /
weapons that I didn't use on level 9.  I made it to the Planes after
killing the Wizard just once more, with one of my 2 wands of death.  I
got to the Earth plane and was all set to use the OoF to find the
portal, except... I didn't have the OoF.  I guess I'll never know what
happened there.  I might have left it with the stuff on lvl9, I guess.
Rats.  At least I hadn't forgotten my wand of wishing!  I wished for
two more gold detection scrolls (I already was carrying two) and a helm
of opposite alignment.  I'd been planning to save my last quickly
accessible wish for a blessed cockatrice corpse or a HoOA, whichever I
needed more, but I'd used it already on scrolls so I decided that I
needed the helm more; it wouldn't rot before I made it through Astral,
and fighting with c-corpses is always scary for me on Astral anyway.
I'm always afraid something weird will happen and bam, I'm gone.  Well,
not gone as such, with  Vlad's AoLS, but whatever.
  Anyway, I sped past Air (with my ring of levitation) without getting
hit.  Seriously.  Not engulfed by any air elementals, or ANYTHING.  A
first for me.  I guess conflict and boots of speed and intrinsic speed
is good, but usually not that good.
  Fire / water were easy, except that on fire it took me about 50 turns
of casting spells and waiting to become confused but not stunned.  I
took a while to get ready on Water, and realized that the wizard was
most likely going to show up again and decided to face him on Water
rather than Astral, so I waited.  He showed, and I WoDeath'd him.
  On Astral the first altar I checked, Famine's, was neutral... the
only one I couldn't ascend at :).  Ah well, went back, deathed Famine
for fun even though I had jumping boots and didn't need to, and blew
past Pestilence to the middle altar.  It was chaotic, and, not having
the OoF, I was actually taking some damage here and there (I had
468/586 health when I ascended, plus my 8 potions of full healing and
AoLS... whatever) so I decided to just use the HoOA and ascend.  I
didn't want to mess tempt fate.  I finished with plenty of everything;
if I'd had to stay on Astral another 1500 turns and face Rodney a
couple more times I could have, especially with the 9 extra blessed
charging scrolls for my 2 wands of death and 8 wands of teleportation,
plus my ring of free action / 5 blessed !oParalysis in case I had to
face Death.

